A||||11||Huck||87 GT vs. 94 Corolla||||1||
Z||000000||Huck||10-30-2001||02:02 AM||||I was returning home sunday morning after a night of drinking, and pulled up to a stoplight on Oxford st. in London... in the lane next to me, a 94 Corolla with rims, soup can exhaust, and nearly a dozen stickers on the door.  I look over at the asian punk driving, and point and laugh at him... (I had to, typical rice rocket!).  The light turns green and off he goes.. so I hammered on it, but didnt really expect him to give er... walked away on me before I knew he was serious..  Next stop light, we're both first ones there...  This time Im ready.  green light, I drop the clutch at about 2500rpm and we're off... right beside me, then slowly starts to pull away... got about 3/4 car length ahead of me once we reached 80km/h(50mph)... I was shocked.. he squacked into second, and I swear I heard him chirp into third.  we drop back down to town speeds... like 65km/h.. we got 1 more light... I wanted to try him one more time.  This time I dump the clutch at 4000rpm... I jet out infront of him, but he catches right back up at the end of 2nd gear... we hit the 80km/h dead even... then backed off.<P>Whats wrong with me?  I thought I should be able to smoke a corolla, but it took everything I had to tie him.  Its an 87 GT 2.8, 138,000km (85,000 miles) with exhaust and a computer chip.. slammed 2", 225 50 r15 all the way around.<P>I was all pumped up, but kinda felt foolish, cause I never did beat him... kinda killed my ego for awhile...<P>A sad day..<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-top||||reg||1
Z||000001||87FieroGTx||10-30-2001||02:16 AM|||| I don't know the Carolla #'s but ANY CAR CAN BE MADE FAST even a family car!<P> Just look at some of the Civic guys they start off with a Slow POS and make a Fast POS!<P> I've even seen a 12 sec Mini Van.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-30-2001||07:31 PM||||Ouch! It does suck to lose a street race to a 4 door family car. Whos know though, maybe all the stickers on his car were things he really had? Some of those ricers are fast, gotta watch out for them.<P>Kind of OT, but I killed a riced out civic last weekend in my SAAB. I dont know what he had all I could see were tinted windows,fart can, and rims. Pulled up to him on a red light, saw him looking at my car. I didnt expect him to race, but he chirped the tires on take off from the light. I just mashed the gas into 1st, (turbo spooling)shifted into 2nd(nice long tire bark) at 6200RPM and he was gone...... He most have felt like and idiot also, bucuase I was driving a big 4 door family auto! Its kind of funny, just because the car has a little "turbo" logo on the back, I allways have people trying to race me. Maybe Ill put a turbo badge on my 84SE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>fun fun!<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000003||artherd||10-30-2001||10:39 PM||||I saw one of these on the street the other night, think I should've raced him?  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/auto-tuning/images/celemai/poze%20mari/renault.jpg"> <P>I don't, here's why  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (PS: please note the torque, it is huge, thank you, goodnight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/auto-tuning/celemai/rapide/renault.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/auto-tuning/celemai/rapide/renault.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||AgaricX||10-30-2001||10:52 PM||||Don't get me wrong... I'm going to get lettring treatment on my rear tailights that says [ I Smoke ] [ Ricers ]... but I've been surprised a couple times by tweaked lawnmowers.  Its usually the Preludes and Accord V6's that do the surprising though.<P>My BIGGEST surprise was a Subaru WRX.  Dropped my jaw, but took him in my 3800SC.  Wish my Fiero had All Wheel Drive too... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||NOS3800||10-31-2001||12:08 AM||||He probably had NOS. At the track I go to, there is a 4 door Honda Accord and a Cavalier Z24. They both spray 75 shots, max for these motors without internal mods. The Accord runs 15.3 with the spray. The Z24 ran 15.0 with spray. WOW! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000006||Huck||10-31-2001||12:34 AM||||It is possible he had nos... I barely noticed a difference in his revs when he chirped into second... I'd have told you guys what stickers he had, but of course, the majority of them were japanise or chinese or somethin like that.  This little escapade will just force me to spend more money on mods than I had originally planned on..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I dont like to lose, even if I am driving a mostly stock car... though I realize no matter how fast you build it, there will always be somebody thats faster... life can be so cruel sometimes!<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-tops||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackStang95||10-31-2001||01:11 AM||||Jap cars that are actually fast can be kinda cool, I've been smoked by a heavy modded eclipse and barely beaten by an accord v-6.  I didn't even try against the twin turbo 300zx I got a light with tonight.  Some beautiful cars there, my friend has one.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Huck||10-31-2001||01:16 AM||||drool.... 300zx.  I saw my cousin at thanksgiving a couple weeks ago, when he pulled up in a 93 300zx.  He let me take it for a boot around Barrie, and he drove my 87 GT around.  I could not believe that car... it is everything I ever wanted my fiero to be.  Meanwhile, he couldnt get over the under steer problems the fiero has compaired to his 300zx.  needless to say, he was in more of a hurry to swap keys back than I was.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-tops||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||10-31-2001||07:27 PM||||Think about it, almost anyone will race something that they think is ricey (if that's even a word), so if you have a decently fast car and rice it out, you basically have a flashy sleeper. If I had to live with an front wheel driver, that's probably what I'd do.||||reg||1
Z||000010||sloth85GT||10-31-2001||11:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>My BIGGEST surprise was a Subaru WRX.  Dropped my jaw, but took him in my 3800SC.  Wish my Fiero had All Wheel Drive too... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah you've gotta watch for those things, they haul A$$!!! 240 turbo horsepower I believe with loads of torque. And added all wheel drive. I wonder what the 1/4 mile time is for those cars. Anyone know?<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
